## PART B — LOCKED RULES (kabhi mat badalna)

Antigravity, ye har variant pe binding hain. Koi bhi rule tootne pe variant reject hoga.

**1. Token-driven from the first line — NO hardcoded values.**
- Har color, radius, shadow, spacing, font `var(--...)` se aaye. Ek bhi hardcoded hex (`#0F5132`),
  hardcoded `border-radius: 8px`, ya hardcoded font-family allowed nahi.
- Standard token names use karo (jo chassis define karta hai): `--primary`, `--secondary`,
  `--surface`, `--bg-base`, `--text-main`, `--text-muted`, `--border`, `--radius-card`,
  `--radius-btn`, `--shadow-md`, `--font-heading`, `--font-body`, `--space-*`.
- **Text color on a colored background** (white text on a green/accent button, announcement bar):
  use `#ffffff` fixed **or** `var(--text-on-accent)` — NEVER `var(--surface)`. (Surface = page/container
  background only. Ye galti pehle ho chuki hai, dobara nahi.)

**2. Structural variants, not cosmetic.**
- Ye variant apne siblings se **layout-level** alag hona chahiye (image placement, columns, stacking,
  grid vs carousel, alignment). Sirf color/spacing ka farak = INVALID variant (woh token layer ka kaam).

**3. Zero fabricated data. Neutral placeholder defaults only.**
- Koi fake naam ("Elena", "Customer Name" chalega but no realistic fake person), fake review text
  ("Add your review here." placeholder chalega), fake ratings, ya fake counts default mein render mat karo.
- Trust signals (stars, "Verified Buyer" badge, review counts) **default mein HIDDEN**, sirf tab render
  hon jab merchant ne real data bhara ho (`is_placeholder`-style guard). Counts/claims settings-driven.

**4. Merchant ke apne products + images pull karo (live Liquid objects).**
- Products/collections/images Shopify objects se aayein: `product.featured_image`, `product.media`,
  `collections[...]`, `product.price` (via `money` filter), etc. Koi hardcoded product/image nahi.
- **Missing-asset fallback:** agar product/image nahi hai, ek **neutral branded placeholder** dikhao
  (no dollar-sign line-art, no client-specific text). Section ko merchant ke actual catalog ke hisaab se
  gracefully adapt karna chahiye (3 products vs 30, images present vs absent).

**5. Responsive — mobile AND desktop, dono properly built.**
- Mobile-first CSS, phir desktop breakpoints. Dono layouts spec ke mutabiq render hon. Tap targets
  mobile pe ≥44px. Ek device pe toota hua variant = INVALID.

**6. CRO-clean structure.**
- Primary CTA above the fold aur clearly visible. Clear visual hierarchy. Agar section conversion-relevant
  hai (hero, product card, grid), CTA/price/add-to-cart prominent hon.

**7. Schema + naming discipline.**
- Har section ka `{% schema %}` complete ho, merchant-editable settings ke saath.
- File naming: `{{SECTION_TYPE}}-v{{N}}.liquid` (e.g. `hero-v3.liquid`). Dependent snippets alag files mein,
  `snippets/` mein, shared aur token-driven.
- Section ke andar scoped CSS `{%- style -%}` block mein, ya shared asset — par colors/tokens
  `theme.liquid` ke `:root` se aayein (asset CSS mein hardcode nahi, warna theme editor live-preview toot-ta hai).

